  - semidefinite programming
  - exhaustive graph enumeration
  - exact certificates
abstract: >-
  Exhaustive enumeration of all connected graphs on up to ten vertices by the
  contextuality gap Delta(G) = theta(G) - alpha(G), with the maximum determined for
  each size and the exact value of the Lovasz theta number established for every
  maximizer by machine-checked primal and dual certificates in exact arithmetic.
  The eight-vertex value, left open by the paper this continues, is the root of
  x^4 - x^3 + 23x^2 - 155x + 158 in the interval (3, 4); its Galois group is the
  full symmetric group on four letters, so the degree cannot be reduced.
